Proposed Note View Design (focused on clean, Apple-like UX that hides complexity while delivering all required functions)
Core Layout (Single Screen)

Top Bar (minimal, always visible)
Search bar (full-text + semantic + tags + OCR)
New Note button (with voice/text/image/handwriting options in a small popover)
View toggle: List / Grid / Graph

Left Sidebar (collapsible)
All Notes
AI Suggested Groups (smart folders created by Knowledge Curator)
Tags / Supertags (flat list + AI-suggested groupings)
Notebooks / Folders (user or AI-created)

Main Content Area (the actual note list)
Notes shown as clean cards in List or Grid view
Each card displays: title, first 2 lines of content or summary, supertags, last updated time
Instant sorting: by date, title, tag, or AI-relevance (one-tap)
Instant filtering via search or tag click

Right Sidebar (contextual, appears when a note is selected)
Full note content with backlinks and related notes
AI Summary + Action Items (auto-generated)
Version history (simple timeline, one-click restore)


Key Interactions (Minimal Friction)

Instant Note Creation:
Tap “New Note” → instantly opens a blank note with cursor ready for typing.
Long-press “New Note” → popover with Voice, Camera (image + OCR), Handwriting, or Text.
Voice note starts recording immediately and auto-transcribes + summarizes.

Collation & Organization:
Drag any note onto another to create a backlink or merge.
Multi-select + “Group as Supertag” or “Move to Notebook”.
AI Suggested Groups appear automatically and can be accepted with one tap.

Search & Retrieval:
Search bar works instantly across all notes (full-text + semantic via pgvector).
Results show highlighted matches and related backlinks.
“Ask your notes” mode: natural language query returns best matching notes + AI summary.

Smart Linking:
While typing, the system suggests relevant existing notes for backlinking (shown as inline chips).
Graph view button shows connected knowledge network (clickable to jump between notes).

AI-Assisted Features:
Every note has an “AI Actions” button: Summarize, Extract Action Items, Create Mind Map, Elaborate.
Contextual suggestions appear as subtle chips above the note (“Add reminder?”, “Link to previous meeting?”).


Accessibility & Simplicity Principles Applied

All actions are one or two taps.
No nested menus or hidden settings in the main flow.
Everything is visible or discoverable without reading documentation.
Heavy operations (OCR, summarization, graph building) happen silently in background via Knowledge Curator.